From 07b3d837e611226175a9f594f0fe829b9851f7ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pieroviano <piero.viano@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 07:47:50 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Add Control bounds-core, scaling and handle-lifecycle
 override surface

Closes API-COMPLETENESS.md P2 item 5 (Control section 5.2). The protected
override points a custom control needs were absent: SetBoundsCore,
SetClientSizeCore, SizeFromClientSize, GetScaledBounds, ScaleControl, ScaleCore,
CreateHandle, DestroyHandle, RecreateHandle - so a subclass could not intercept
sizing, DPI/font scaling or handle recreation.

SetBounds now routes through SetBoundsCore (the WinForms structure) so overriding
that one method sees every bounds change; the existing equality-based specified
handling becomes flag-based, which is behaviour-equivalent for the standard
BoundsSpecified values and correct for arbitrary combinations. GetScaledBounds
scales location and size independently per specified; ScaleControl funnels through
SetBoundsCore; RecreateHandle destroys then creates via guarded GTK realize/
unrealize.

Covered by ControlScalingFunctionalTests: SetBounds->SetBoundsCore routing,
scaling arithmetic (all-components and specified-only), SizeFromClientSize
identity, ScaleControl funnelling, and RecreateHandle ordering. Full Forms suite
green at 2465.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
